Package: mfbdfm
Type: Package
Title: Mixed-Frequency Bayesian Dynamic Factor Model
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Philipp", "Kronenberg", email = "philippkronenberg@gmx.ch",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates a Bayesian dynamic factor model that integrates
    weekly, monthly and quarterly data by extracting a single dynamic
    factor. Missing and mixed-frequency observations are handled through
    data augmentation, the factor state equation includes stochastic
    volatility to capture crisis-period fluctuations, and serial
    correlation in measurement errors is removed by quasi-differencing.
    An identification restriction can fix the factor's loading on a chosen
    target series so it is directly interpretable as that series' growth
    rate. The package ships a flagship application, the Weekly Activity
    Index (WAI), a high-frequency indicator of Swiss gross domestic
    product (GDP) anchored to GDP growth, along with tools for real-time
    GDP vintage handling, out-of-sample forecast evaluation, and the
    tables and plots used in the accompanying analysis. Methodology and empirical results are
    described in Kronenberg (2026) <doi:10.1186/s41937-026-00157-w>, which
    extends the mixed-frequency framework of Eckert, Kronenberg, Mikosch
    and Neuwirth (2025) <doi:10.1002/jae.3104>.
